## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend Core & API Contracts (`app/`)

Implement the 7 verified backend modifications (B1–B7) required for robust, secure mobile BYOD and web intake.

#### [MODIFY] [encounter.py](file:///home/conste/repos/pts/app/schemas/encounter.py)
- Update `EncounterBootstrapRequest` to support `channel: Literal["kiosk", "android_byod", "mobile_byod", "ivr_phone", "web_kiosk"]` with alias `device_channel`.
- Add `patient_id` as an optional parameter alongside `qr_token`.
- Add `bearer_token: str` to `EncounterBootstrapResponse` (B1).

#### [MODIFY] [encounters.py](file:///home/conste/repos/pts/app/api/encounters.py)
- **B1**: Issue a short-lived opaque encounter bearer token on `bootstrap`, stored with 30-minute TTL. Validate token on encounter-scoped operations.
- **B4**: Handle `mobile_byod` and resolve patient identity via `patient_id` or `qr_token`.
- **B6**: Extend `GET /api/encounters/{id}` to return full rehydration state (facts, turn progress, attached documents, triage severity, call session).
- **B7**: Add `POST /api/encounters/{id}/consent` endpoint receiving `{granted_at, language, consent_version, channel}` and persisting a DPDP audit record.

#### [MODIFY] [call_sessions.py](file:///home/conste/repos/pts/app/api/call_sessions.py) & [call_session.py](file:///home/conste/repos/pts/app/schemas/call_session.py)
- **B3**: Write synthesized TTS audio turn files to `./static/audio/` and return `next_question_audio_url` in `AudioTurnResponse` alongside `next_question_audio_base64`.

#### [MODIFY] [documents.py](file:///home/conste/repos/pts/app/api/documents.py)
- **B2**: Ensure both single document upload (`POST /api/documents/upload`) and batch upload consistently return `extracted_medications`, `flagged_interactions`, and `highlighted_image_url` for patient verification.

#### [NEW] [idempotency.py](file:///home/conste/repos/pts/app/core/middleware/idempotency.py)
- **B5**: Fast idempotent request interceptor checking `Idempotency-Key` header on mutating calls (`bootstrap`, `audio-turn`, `documents/upload`), storing key-to-response mappings in SQLite for 24h to prevent duplicate records during flaky mobile reconnections.

